{"chunk_id": "5a8662db8f80", "text": "Satyavan returns late with Savitri, prompting the forest sages to question him and the royal family. Unaware of what truly happened, Satyavan explains he had fallen asleep in the woods after a sudden pain. At the sages\u2019 urging, Savitri reveals the truth: the sage Narada had foretold Satyavan\u2019s death, and when Yama came to take his soul, she followed and won five boons through her devotion and wisdom\u2014restoring her father\u2011in\u2011law Dyumatsena\u2019s sight and kingdom, granting sons to her father and herself, and ultimately securing Satyavan\u2019s long life. The sages praise her chastity and virtue for rescuing the royal line from ruin. Soon after, news arrives that Dyumatsena\u2019s usurper has been killed, allowing him to reclaim his throne. The episode celebrates Savitri\u2019s steadfast devotion and portrays righteous virtue as powerful enough to overturn fate and restore an entire dynasty.\nSavitri reveals how she won boons from Yama restoring Satyavan and Dyumatsena; the king regains his throne, fulfilling her vows and prosperity for both families.\nThemes: devotion and marital fidelity, divine boons and fate, restoration of kingship, ascetic witness and praise", "vector": [0.01102356519550085, -0.027609173208475113, -0.0029317992739379406, 0.021578043699264526, -0.016913969069719315, 0.019487250596284866, -0.005964117590337992, -0.01805318333208561, -0.021819287911057472, -0.017463471740484238, 0.02444618009030819, 0.018415050581097603, 0.019782107323408127, 0.0033958612475544214, -0.006349439732730389, 0.007947688922286034, 0.04647991061210632, 0.011740599758923054, 0.027073072269558907, -0.029190668836236, 0.007404887583106756, -0.008343063294887543, -0.016351062804460526, 0.032085612416267395, -0.016833554953336716, 0.018254220485687256, 0.017959365621209145, -0.0300484299659729, 0.018750112503767014, -0.012028753757476807, -0.02660398557782173, -0.009274537675082684, -0.01101016253232956, -0.031335